From 4617a7bbc6ce088b0fcf4afda9eda56d36933438 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frederik Richter <frederik.richter@mailbox.org>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:55:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(config/render): unify sdr and hdr brightness settings in
 monitor definition

- Add hdrbrightness monitor rule setting to scale HDR content brightness on HDR monitors
- Add unified brightness monitor rule setting to adjust both SDR and HDR brightness simultaneously
- Add Lua config bindings and legacy ConfigManager (monitor and monitorv2) bindings for brightness and hdrbrightness
- Fall back to active monitor rule in hl.monitor when no rule exists for output
- Expose brightness, sdr_brightness, and hdr_brightness on Lua HL.Monitor object
- Fix skipCM in OpenGL renderToFBInternal bypassing shader brightness scaling for HDR surfaces on HDR outputs
- Avoid redundant applyCMType calls in applyMonitorRuleSoft when only brightness/saturation changes
- Fix min brightness (0.0) making the screen completely black instead of jumping to 100%
- Fix direct scanout bypassing HDR brightness scaling
- Fix targetImageDescription check in Renderer getCMSettings
- Remove corrupting maxLuminance scaling that threw off tonemapper calculations
- Guard blurprepare against division by zero when brightness is zero
- Validate non-negative and finite brightness values in parsers and bindings
- Expose hdrBrightness in hyprctl monitors JSON and text outputs
- Expand unit test coverage in tests/config/MonitorParser.cpp
